routerd2 native DS-Lite endpoint resolver

This package is original routerd2 code under the repository's BSD-3-Clause
license. Protocol references are RFC 6333, RFC 1035, RFC 2181 and RFC 3596.
No external AFTR client daemon, old command runner, or shell implementation is
copied or executed by this package.

The comparative routerd source used to identify legacy Linux behavior is:
  repository: https://github.com/imksoo/routerd
  revision: 1329ef54f296507eda79bbbc3b853783dd27251e

In particular, the active Linux controller and the separate FreeBSD apply
helper have different AFTR selection behavior. The README records the audit
and the intentional bounded-lifetime/bootstrap differences. This notice does
not claim full legacy feature compatibility.

The miekg/dns library supplies DNS message encoding and UDP/TCP exchange.
golang.org/x/sys supplies Linux socket options and boot-clock access. Their
licenses are distributed through the repository's dependency license-manifest
process. Network namespace and netlink operations in integration tests are
fixture-only; the production resolver never mutates or inspects host network
configuration.
